03:14:01 <elliott> Notes to time travelling ips:
03:14:01 <elliott> Usage of time travel can be very punishing on the performance of the funge interpreter. If travel is performed to the past, the interpreter must be capable of reproducing all conditions that existed at the destination time, which includes all ips, stacks, and funge space cells. Some interpreters may only store time snapshots from only so far back (The furthest point in the past that can be jumped to can be determined with the P command).
03:14:05 <elliott> Some interpreters CHEAT
03:14:30 <Deewiant> CCBI does what I think is reasonable: it allows you to travel back up to the time when you loaded TRDS, but not before
03:14:49 <Deewiant> That way TRDS has very little performance impact unless you actually use it.
